00:13:46,080 --> 00:13:50,160
Everyone aboard this ship is
aware of that cruel reality.

255
00:13:53,320 --> 00:13:54,520
What's with you?

256
00:13:54,880 --> 00:13:56,292
Chill out, sweetie baby.

257
00:13:56,600 --> 00:13:58,835
I'm just trying to show you some love.

258
00:14:00,280 --> 00:14:01,680
Hey, come on.

259
00:14:01,980 --> 00:14:03,880
Quit moving around so much.

260
00:14:04,020 --> 00:14:06,417
Can't you see I'm trying
to read these messages?

261
00:14:06,500 --> 00:14:08,440
At 9.25 this morning,

262
00:14:08,600 --> 00:14:10,637
officials at the prison
in Naples were shocked

263
00:14:10,720 --> 00:14:13,460
to discover that Polpo
had shot himself dead?

264
00:14:14,280 --> 00:14:15,520
Shit on a stick.

265
00:14:15,780 --> 00:14:18,677
I thought for sure Popo
would be the girl's guardian.

266
00:14:18,760 --> 00:14:20,700
If it's not him, who is it then?

267
00:14:21,580 --> 00:14:25,521
Who'd stick their neck out to look
after that disappearing actress?

268
00:14:31,020 --> 00:14:32,667
Well, I better get after it.

269
00:14:33,880 --> 00:14:35,080
Find them, eh?

270
00:14:35,660 --> 00:14:38,836
Who would be more capable
of protecting her than Popo?

271
00:14:39,360 --> 00:14:41,317
They definitely have to be a couple.

272
00:14:41,400 --> 00:14:44,517
No one else would be assigned
to such an important job.

273
00:14:44,600 --> 00:14:47,380
Them being a stand user
is also a no-brainer.

274
00:14:48,040 --> 00:14:51,660
The question is, who the
hell checks all those boxes?

275
00:15:04,240 --> 00:15:05,260
Groceries, check.

276
00:15:06,660 --> 00:15:08,740
Surroundings clear. Let's see.

277
00:15:09,880 --> 00:15:13,280
So I'm supposed to go through
here, make a turn there,

278
00:15:13,580 --> 00:15:17,580
end up back on this street, and
then head in the opposite direction.

279
00:15:17,760 --> 00:15:18,720
Right. Nice.

280
00:15:25,500 --> 00:15:26,912
Narancia, you listening?

281
00:15:27,360 --> 00:15:31,197
That's a list of groceries from the
group, along with everything else we need.

282
00:15:31,280 --> 00:15:33,360
And these are the keys to the car.

283
00:15:33,680 --> 00:15:34,600
Now listen up.

284
00:15:34,800 --> 00:15:36,180
I have faith in you.

285
00:15:36,460 --> 00:15:38,342
This will be a walk in the park.

286
00:15:40,340 --> 00:15:41,170
One more thing.

287
00:15:41,253 --> 00:15:44,612
No one has the faintest idea
our group is hiding out here.

288
00:15:44,740 --> 00:15:47,597
Not even the vintners out front
are aware of our presence.

289
00:15:47,680 --> 00:15:50,417
When you're done with the shopping,
I want you to retrace your path,

290
00:15:50,500 --> 00:15:53,618
then do it again more times
than you think necessary.

291
00:15:53,840 --> 00:15:56,311
Also, make a U-turn every once in a while.

292
00:15:56,440 --> 00:15:59,397
That way you'll know whether
anyone is tailing you.

293
00:15:59,480 --> 00:16:03,157
After that, I want you to take the
car I left for you in the parking lot.

294
00:16:03,240 --> 00:16:05,946
Then and only then do I
want you to come home.

295
00:16:06,200 --> 00:16:10,257
No one should have any inkling that
we're looking after the boss's daughter.

296
00:16:10,340 --> 00:16:13,357
But just in case someone
does know what we're up to,

297
00:16:13,440 --> 00:16:16,477
this runaround strategy should
keep them off our trail.

298
00:16:16,560 --> 00:16:17,390
You understand?

299
00:16:17,473 --> 00:16:19,420
We need the things on the list.

300
00:16:19,620 --> 00:16:21,032
That much is still true.

301
00:16:21,200 --> 00:16:25,200
However, it's absolutely imperative
that nobody finds our hideout!

302
00:16:25,380 --> 00:16:26,210
You're crying out loud!

303
00:16:26,293 --> 00:16:27,380
I get it! I get it!

304
00:16:27,580 --> 00:16:29,227
Just leave everything to me!

305
00:16:29,400 --> 00:16:33,620
Alright, now repeat everything we
just discussed, start to finish. Huh?

306
00:16:34,020 --> 00:16:35,597
Well, uh...

307
00:16:35,680 --> 00:16:40,504
I buy all the stuff on the list, then drive
around and around in a field, until...

308
00:16:41,320 --> 00:16:42,637
That's the wrong answer!

309
00:16:42,720 --> 00:16:44,497
Quit screwing around and get serious!

310
00:16:44,580 --> 00:16:46,617
Now tell me what I said
from the beginning!

311
00:16:46,700 --> 00:16:48,097
You told me to...

312
00:16:48,180 --> 00:16:51,180
drive around an empty
lot so I don't get dizzy!

313
00:16:52,340 --> 00:16:54,377
What the hell is wrong with you?!

314
00:16:54,460 --> 00:16:55,997
Are you seeing this, Abbacchio?

315
00:16:56,080 --> 00:16:58,577
Tell him to stop stabbing
me with the damn keys!

316
00:16:58,660 --> 00:17:02,217
I never should have put him in charge
of shopping in the first place!

317
00:17:02,300 --> 00:17:06,947
Whether you two man-babies want to keep
playing with keys is your own business.

318
00:17:07,220 --> 00:17:09,926
As for me, I'm interested
in Narancia's stand.

319
00:17:10,260 --> 00:17:14,017
If we're being followed, he'll put
an end to them before they know it.

320
00:17:14,100 --> 00:17:16,865
That's why Bucciarati
gave him the task he did.

321
00:17:17,520 --> 00:17:21,980
Long story short, I need to get my
ass back here without a soul knowing.

322
00:17:22,260 --> 00:17:23,580
No stalkers allowed!

323
00:17:30,540 --> 00:17:31,481
Something's off.

324
00:17:32,080 --> 00:17:35,757
my eyes tell me I'm all
by myself but my gut says

325
00:17:35,840 --> 00:17:40,857
otherwise and if that wasn't
bad enough this car Fugo got me

326
00:17:40,940 --> 00:17:47,757
has given off some bad vibes
too come on now already

327
00:17:47,840 --> 00:17:52,760
I'm dying to know where oh
where could you be heading to

328
00:17:53,580 --> 00:17:54,410
Narancia?

329
00:17:55,100 --> 00:17:56,360
It came from here.

330
00:18:02,900 --> 00:18:06,253
Now, like I said, where are
you running off to, stranger?

331
00:18:06,800 --> 00:18:08,377
You keep looking behind you.

332
00:18:08,460 --> 00:18:12,048
Worried some big bad boogeyman
is following you or something?

333
00:18:12,680 --> 00:18:13,857
Just who the hell do you think you are?

334
00:18:13,940 --> 00:18:15,293
Don't you act so scary?

335
00:18:15,380 --> 00:18:17,977
Is that how you treat
someone asking you something?

336
00:18:18,060 --> 00:18:21,657
I didn't realize you'd be so rude,
answering a question with a question.

337
00:18:21,740 --> 00:18:23,017
Shut your face, freak!

338
00:18:23,100 --> 00:18:25,276
I want you out of this car right now!

339
00:18:25,600 --> 00:18:27,424
This isn't getting us anywhere.

340
00:18:27,720 --> 00:18:29,320
You can call me Formaggio.

341
00:18:29,660 --> 00:18:31,320
I'm part of the Familia.

342
00:18:32,120 --> 00:18:35,480
You are aware that Polpo
passed last night, aren't you?

343
00:18:36,140 --> 00:18:37,600
This sucks ass.

344
00:18:37,800 --> 00:18:38,637
Your trusty team...

345
00:18:38,720 --> 00:18:39,550
Merida!

346
00:18:39,633 --> 00:18:40,860
Talk about bad news!

347
00:18:41,120 --> 00:18:44,637
I don't know how this guy found out
about our mission, but he's on to us.

348
00:18:44,720 --> 00:18:45,550
Just great.

349
00:18:45,740 --> 00:18:47,505
I wonder if he's a stand user.

350
00:18:49,120 --> 00:18:51,117
Naracha, this is the rudest welcome ever.

351
00:18:51,200 --> 00:18:52,300
What gives, amigo?

352
00:18:52,800 --> 00:18:55,741
Where's Bucciarati and the
rest of your playmates?

353
00:18:56,360 --> 00:18:57,620
No clue, friend.

354
00:18:57,980 --> 00:18:59,317
How should I know where they are?

355
00:18:59,400 --> 00:19:00,437
I'm not their keeper.

356
00:19:00,520 --> 00:19:02,197
Did you check the restaurants around here?

357
00:19:02,280 --> 00:19:05,017
This car you're using,
it's a rental, isn't it?

358
00:19:05,100 --> 00:19:07,020
And Bucciarati is the renter.

359
00:19:07,420 --> 00:19:11,220
Why would you be in this car if
you weren't aware of that? Well?

360
00:19:12,500 --> 00:19:14,540
I always drive around in his cars.

361
00:19:14,660 --> 00:19:15,717
Everyone knows that.

362
00:19:15,800 --> 00:19:18,500
I'm 17, so I clearly don't have my own.

363
00:19:18,900 --> 00:19:20,606
That's why I'm borrowing his.

364
00:19:21,620 --> 00:19:22,700
Hmm. Oh, yeah.

365
00:19:22,960 --> 00:19:24,137
Did you hear the news?

366
00:19:24,220 --> 00:19:27,177
Polpo's colossal corpse
is causing the mortician

367
00:19:27,260 --> 00:19:29,517
trouble because he doesn't
know how to torch the thing.

368
00:19:29,600 --> 00:19:32,482
There's no way to squeeze
him into the damn oven.

369
00:19:33,920 --> 00:19:37,685
Guess he'll just have to hack
that fat calzone into tiny pieces.

370
00:19:43,060 --> 00:19:44,800
You shut up! What?

371
00:19:45,020 --> 00:19:47,079
Aren't you thinking the same thing?

372
00:19:49,260 --> 00:19:50,300
Huh? What?

373
00:19:50,540 --> 00:19:51,893
Who are you talking to?

374
00:19:55,280 --> 00:19:57,740
Wow, you totally fell for it.

375
00:19:57,900 --> 00:19:59,606
You're such a disappointment.

376
00:20:00,020 --> 00:20:01,100
Say no, aren't ya?

377
00:20:01,400 --> 00:20:02,812
Answer something for me.

378
00:20:03,120 --> 00:20:06,997
Why are you fools nowhere to be seen
while a capo is being laid to rest?

379
00:20:07,080 --> 00:20:08,551
Get to snitching already.

380
00:20:08,740 --> 00:20:11,217
I don't have all day to
follow your ass around.

381
00:20:11,300 --> 00:20:14,037
When I'm finished, kid, you
won't have a secret left.

382
00:20:14,120 --> 00:20:15,720
Eat shit. Huh?

383
00:20:17,440 --> 00:20:18,480
Better yet...

384
00:20:19,240 --> 00:20:20,220
Drop dead!

385
00:20:30,120 --> 00:20:31,440
What is that thing?

386
00:20:31,840 --> 00:20:32,780
Lil' bomber!

387
00:20:34,240 --> 00:20:35,800
So he's a stand user.

388
00:20:36,020 --> 00:20:37,138
Get him, tiny feet!

389
00:20:42,840 --> 00:20:43,840
Damn you!

390
00:20:44,300 --> 00:20:46,437
Look at what you did to me, bastardo!

391
00:20:46,520 --> 00:20:47,350
I'm bleeding!

392
00:20:47,600 --> 00:20:48,840
How dare you hurt me!

393
00:20:53,060 --> 00:20:53,890
Frickin' hell!

394
00:20:54,020 --> 00:20:55,196
This guy's a psycho!

395
00:20:57,620 --> 00:21:00,620
Die, die, die, die! Damn!

396
00:21:01,000 --> 00:21:01,941
He doesn't quit!

397
00:21:02,160 --> 00:21:03,278
I'll slaughter you!

398
00:21:05,120 --> 00:21:07,637
This crazy kid's
completely blown a gasket.

399
00:21:07,720 --> 00:21:10,117
He's shooting everything
in sight like a madman.

400
00:21:10,200 --> 00:21:13,435
And I'm stuck inside this
tin can with nowhere to hide!

401
00:21:13,640 --> 00:21:15,816
Staying in this car's gonna do me in!

402
00:21:18,260 --> 00:21:19,090
That's...

403
00:21:19,173 --> 00:21:20,003
the bomb!

404
00:21:20,086 --> 00:21:21,660
Blow him away, little bummer!

405
00:21:24,020 --> 00:21:25,255
How do you like that?

406
00:21:25,380 --> 00:21:26,377
Did it feel good?

407
00:21:26,460 --> 00:21:27,920
You a pile of ash yet?

408
00:21:30,140 --> 00:21:31,960
Damn it! We get him?

409
00:21:32,560 --> 00:21:34,080
What? Where'd he go?

410
00:21:34,560 --> 00:21:37,017
Did the blast knock him
into the stratosphere?

411
00:21:37,100 --> 00:21:39,453
No, but there's not a piece of him left!

412
00:21:40,380 --> 00:21:41,320
Where'd he go?

413
00:21:42,720 --> 00:21:44,520
You're so oblivious, kid.

414
00:21:44,780 --> 00:21:46,309
I'm right under your nose.

415
00:21:47,460 --> 00:21:49,460
I can micrify myself.

416
00:21:49,860 --> 00:21:52,120
That's my very secret weapon!

417
00:21:53,480 --> 00:21:58,800
My stand is called Tiny Feet, and all the
other guys said it wasn't worth anything.

418
00:22:00,180 --> 00:22:02,937
They can talk shit till
they're blue in the face,

419
00:22:03,020 --> 00:22:05,860
but personal talent is
all about how you use it.

420
00:22:06,060 --> 00:22:07,080
What the hell?

421
00:22:07,340 --> 00:22:08,811
I don't see him anywhere!

422
00:22:08,980 --> 00:22:10,160
This is ridiculous!

423
00:22:10,580 --> 00:22:11,992
How'd he just disappear?

424
00:22:12,260 --> 00:22:13,140
Is he here?

425
00:22:13,880 --> 00:22:17,297
The same damn thing happened when
he first showed up in the car.

426
00:22:17,380 --> 00:22:20,317
You can look around to your
heart's content I'm gonna

427
00:22:20,400 --> 00:22:23,753
buy some time while you parade
around looking like a fool

428
00:22:27,700 --> 00:22:28,800
It's a chick.

429
00:22:29,040 --> 00:22:32,275
What do you know the bastards
buying stuff for a chick?

430
00:22:32,480 --> 00:22:36,656
He's got nylons and lipstick in there
There's even some designer blush.

431
00:22:36,920 --> 00:22:41,740
Who's all this shit for this
kagakatsu's mom is big sis

432
00:22:42,400 --> 00:22:43,230
No way.

433
00:22:43,500 --> 00:22:45,897
Women are super picky
about stuff like this.

434
00:22:45,980 --> 00:22:47,897
They buy their own makeup and clothes.

435
00:22:47,980 --> 00:22:51,637
The only chick who can trust a
guy with this kind of thing is one

436
00:22:51,720 --> 00:22:54,957
who thinks they would be in mortal
danger if they went outside.

437
00:22:55,040 --> 00:22:56,900
This all stinks to high heaven.

438
00:22:57,420 --> 00:23:00,557
It's looking like my instincts
were spot on after all.

439
00:23:00,640 --> 00:23:04,717
The ones chosen to protect the boss's
daughter was Bucerati and his back scratchers.

440
00:23:04,800 --> 00:23:05,859
It has to be them.

441
00:23:06,700 --> 00:23:08,577
I will find their hiding place.

442
00:23:08,660 --> 00:23:11,836
And the best part is, Narachi
is going to show me how.

443
00:23:12,020 --> 00:23:15,480
My power should be working
its magic on him any second.

444
00:23:18,480 --> 00:23:21,245
That bastard's got to be
around here somewhere.

445
00:23:21,680 --> 00:23:24,739
I know he's waiting to
follow me back to the others.

446
00:23:24,840 --> 00:23:25,840
Let him try.

447
00:23:26,420 --> 00:23:29,297
I'm going to shake off this
stalker and get back to base.

448
00:23:29,380 --> 00:23:31,797
And if he tries to get
in my way, he's dead.

449
00:23:31,880 --> 00:23:33,580
This mission is in the bag.

450
00:24:08,660 --> 00:24:09,490
You
